text:
kevin: pushed an Astro + LlamaIndex starter that demos embeddings + a tiny eval harness. When running locally the embed call from the client works, but on Netlify preview it fails with CORS and some weird token leak warnings. repo: https://github.com/redwood-inference/astro-llama-starter
leah: quick question — are you calling the embeddings endpoint directly from the browser?
kevin: yeah to keep the demo minimal. code: ```js
// src/lib/embed.js (client)
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk'
const c = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: import.meta.env.PUBLIC_REDWOOD_KEY })
export async function embed(text){
  return c.embeddings.create({ model: 'e2-mini', input: text })
}
```
ashwin: there are two problems: 1) PUBLIC_* keys are exposed to the browser. 2) many hosts block outbound auth headers in certain preview environments causing a CORS-like failure and noisy retries in the SDK. The embed path is also throttled which makes retries look worse.
leah: agree — for a demo we should proxy via a serverless function so the key stays secret and we control CORS. Example pattern: 
```js
// functions/embed.js (server)
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk'
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY })
export async function handler(req){
  const out = await client.embeddings.create({ model: 'e2-mini', input: req.body.text })
  return new Response(JSON.stringify(out))
}
```
kevin: ok makes sense. I moved the call server-side and switched to REDWOOD_API_KEY. Netlify preview now returns 200.
ashwin: small DX note: we should also update the starter README to show both patterns (client vs server) and strongly recommend server-side for any real key. And add a tiny CI smoke test that runs the eval harness against the serverless endpoint with a stubbed client so preview builds catch CORS/auth regressions.
leah: can we also add a lint rule to flag import.meta.env.PUBLIC_* when used to construct RedwoodClient? Would be neat.
kevin: opening PR with changes: serverless proxy, README note, a Jest smoke test, and a linter rule. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/astro-llama-starter/pull/3 :sparkles: 
devex-bot: Created issue #29 in astro-llama-starter: "avoid PUBLIC keys in sample apps; proxy embeddings via serverless function + add CI smoke test"
kevin: thanks all, tests passing in CI, eval harness is running in the PR pipeline. closing loop.
